      "tree_id": "74e3b6688f3e5648fdf23c87d96aa4d4f95f9c51",
      "message": "feat: unify Phoenix listeners and embed the Gateway runtime (#4)\n\nOne Phoenix Endpoint can now own H1/H2 and explicitly enabled H3 through\none ListenerSet and core instance. A reusable `Gaoxy.Proxy.Gateway` owns\nmanaged upstreams, shared route generations, reload receipts,\naccepted-configuration recovery and shutdown; standalone JSON v1\ndelegates to it. Supported staged core activation replaces private\nInstance startup, and opt-in readiness-aware Alt-Svc covers secure final\nresponses before header budget checks.\n\nThe five distributions and standalone application are prepared as 0.8.0.\nOptional H3 and package boundaries remain intact. CI and the\nexact-source release workflow now include isolated Gateway consumers and\nactual unified Phoenix browser acceptance.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Exact ordinary compatibility/composition gate: 265 executed, zero\nfailures/exclusions/skips.\n- Actual Phoenix H1/H2/H3 browser/peer gate: 8 PASS checks, native H2/H3\nWebSockets, reload/restoration and clean exit.\n- Isolated core/HTTP/Gateway/H3-Gateway consumers passed; five actual\npackage archives match all 122 runtime payload files.\n- Strict production compilation, formatting, 9 packaging regressions and\nstandalone core/Gateway/H3 release smokes passed.\n- Independent specification, code and release-preparation reviews\npassed.\n\nElixir 1.20 strict compilation exposed two unreachable outer reload\nerror clauses. The two-clause removal preserves the inner missing-set\nhandling and public invalid-options guard; independent review,\nGateway/lifecycle 20/0 and a fresh committed-source 265/0 gate pass.\nInitial hosted failures are preserved; corrected-source hosted checks\nremain required.\n\nCommands, immutable logs, source hashes and known baseline failures are\nrecorded in `docs/acceptance/unified-listeners-embedded-gateway.md`.\nSpecialist pressure/soak testing and deployment retain their existing\nscope boundaries.",
